icon "banner.tga"
description "A Cheats section in the Game Menu, for the player whose turn it is. Resources gives 10 or 100 of any resource, one resource per click, or 5000 of every resource at once. Units lists the units of the player's class and of its commanders' summoning rituals; click one, then a seen map square, to place 1 or 10 of it there. Restore movement: click a map square, and every unit there gets its action points back. Reveal Map puts every square of every plane in view until the next turn, as the Game Over screen's Reveal Map does. Events lists every enabled mod's events, with a search; click one to run it with its triggers skipped, a square event on the next map square clicked. Teleport, a line under the selected commander's orders on the map: click it, then a seen square on any plane, and the commander and his troops teleport there for no action points; landing on enemies starts a battle, as walking in does. Mod Settings can turn the Teleport line off. A Lua script; needs CoE5SE from Nexus Mods."
needs_script_extender
# CoE5SE takes the line above and does nothing with it. Without CoE5SE running, the game stops at
# it with its Mod Error, which names the line, instead of loading this mod without CoE5SE.
